# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Build output -- packs are published as release assets, not committed
dist/
web/data/

# PyInstaller desktop build (tools/build_desktop.py). Binaries are release
# assets built by CI on each platform, never committed -- and a locally built
# one may have been built with --include-local, which must never be shared.
build/
*.spec

# Generated static course pages: 391 files rebuilt from the pack by
# `npm run site`, and by CI before every Pages deploy. Committing them would
# mean shipping build output that silently drifts from the data it was built
# from -- and the drift is invisible in review, because a stale page looks
# exactly like a fresh one.
web/site/
web/sitemap.txt
web/robots.txt

node_modules/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Never commit anything a user typed. There should be nothing to commit,
# because PathAhead does not write user data anywhere -- this is belt and
# braces for anyone experimenting locally.
*.profile.json
profiles/
logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL-ONLY DATA OVERLAYS -- never published, and the reason is legal, not
# tidiness.
#
# Some figures a family wants are published by MOE, SEAB or an institution
# under terms that let anyone READ them but reserve the right to reproduce
# them. PathAhead's public build therefore carries none of those figures and
# links the reader to the primary source instead (see
# tools/build_secondary_schools_pack.py and docs/LOCAL_DATA.md).
#
# An individual may still keep a personal copy for their own private study.
# If one exists here, the build picks it up and the corresponding feature
# lights up locally. These patterns exist so that a personal copy can never
# become a published one by way of a `git add -A` at the wrong moment.
#
# Anything under a `local/` directory inside a pack is covered, so a new
# overlay added later is ignored by default rather than by remembering to
# come back here.
packs/*/local/
packs/**/local/
local-data/
*.local.json
*.local.yaml

# The compiled pack is a build artifact -- but note it is ALSO the file that
# would carry a local overlay's figures if one were present. Ignored twice
# over for that reason: once as build output above (dist/, web/data/), and
# named again here so the reason is not lost if that comment is ever edited.
web/data/singapore.json
